<title>MEXICO: Mexico's ICA Q1 net sharply down.</title>
<headline>Mexico's ICA Q1 net sharply down.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican builder Empresas ICA said on Monday its net profit for the first quarter totaled 52 million pesos compared with 280 million pesos in the same period the year before.</p>
<p>Earnings per share for the first three months of the year were 0.49 peso, versus 2.69 pesos in 1996, the company said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The builder said its gross margins improved to 22 percent from 16 percent in 1996, citing a better mix of high margin projects despite lower revenue from heavy and industrial construction.</p>
<p>			     Q1 1997			Q1 1996</p>
<p>     Shr			   0.49		     2.69</p>
<p>     Net		    51.83 million	     280.08 million</p>
<p>     Revs		   1.652 bln		2.206 bln</p>
<p>     Gross profit	349.51 million	     353.65 million</p>
<p>     Oper Income	 106.39 million	     112.42 million</p>
<p>     Integ fin  gain   152.21 million    gain   499.85 million</p>
<p>	    Int paid     374.81 million			n/a</p>
<p>	    FX loss	 36.58 million			n/a</p>
<p>	    Int earned   333.65 million			n/a</p>
<p>	    Mon gain     229.95 million			n/a</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures in Mexican pesos.</p>
<p>Full company name is Empresas ICA Sociedad Controladora SA de CV.</p>
<p>((-- Daniel Perez-Whitaker, Monterrey bureau +528 3457617))</p>
</text>
